 "response": "Thebreta's budget is now **$2,308K**. I worked this out by hand over about 1,600 records, so there is some room for arithmetic error.\n\n**Method**\n1. Only Finance Office records count. Messages from Operations, Marketing, Legal, Vendor, PMO, Facilities, Sales and Engineering are ignored. Finance Office notes that don't change the budget (rooms, audits, purchase orders) are also ignored.\n2. I resolved every withdrawal chain from the latest record backwards. A withdrawal only takes effect if no later active withdrawal cancels it. Examples:\n   - #5 (+$59K) stays. The chain is #998 \u2192 #510 \u2192 #111 \u2192 #42 \u2192 #21 \u2192 #15 \u2192 #5, and with #998 active, the withdrawal of #5 is itself cancelled.\n   - #10 (\u2212$164K) stays. In the chain #1563 \u2192 #1176 \u2192 #1009 \u2192 #538 \u2192 #69 \u2192 #20 \u2192 #10, #20's withdrawal of #10 ends up cancelled.\n   - #17 (+$449K) is removed. In the chain #1058 \u2192 #71 \u2192 #60 \u2192 #52 \u2192 #34 \u2192 #17, #34 stays active and withdraws #17.\n   - #125 (+$91K) is removed. In the chain #991 \u2192 #981 \u2192 #300 \u2192 #261 \u2192 #132 \u2192 #125, #132 stays active and withdraws #125.\n   - #900 (\u2212$468K) is removed. #1364 cancels #1090, so #1085's withdrawal of #900 stands.\n3. Starting from the $2,450K set in #0001, I applied every Finance Office increase and decrease that remained active, in record order.\n\nANSWER: $2308K",
